  "english": "22. Tuesday. [Of] Vahan of Goghtn, and [not 21].\nOf Eugene the Virgin, etc.\n24. Thursday. [Of] Tryphon, Parsam, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n26. Saturday. [Of] Athanasius and Cyril the Patriarchs.\n27. Sunday. Second [Sunday]. Tone 6 [gki]. Father (Harts): \"Today he is sacrificed\" (Aysor zenou).\n28. Monday. [Of] Eugenius, Macarius, etc.\n29. Tuesday. [Of] Andrew the General and his army, etc.\n31. Thursday. [Of] Adrianus and his wife Anatolia, etc.\n\nFebruary\n\n2. Saturday. [Of] Gregory the Theologian.\n3. Sunday. Third [Sunday]. Barekendan of the Fast of Catechumens.\n12. Tuesday. [Of] the Sukiasank [Sukias and companions], and [of] the Voskian priests.\n14. Thursday. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\n24. Sunday. Tone 8 [dki]. Great Barekendan [of Great Lent]. See also the others in the First Volume up to Vardavar, keeping the order of this place.\n\nApril\n\n7. Sunday. Tone 2 [aki]. Palm Sunday, and the Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n14. Sunday. Tone 1 [adz]. Easter: Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See also the others according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nMay\n\n23. Thursday. Tone 8 [dki]. Ascension of Christ.\n\nJune\n\n2. Sunday. Tone 2 [aki]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost].\nBarekendan of the Elijah Fast.\n9. Sunday. Tone 1 [adz]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Father (Harts) Tone 1 [adz]: \"Who came for the salvation of the universe\" (Or ekir i prkutiun tiezerats).\n\nJuly\n\n14. Sunday. Tone 4 [bki]. Sixth [Sunday]. Father (Harts) Tone 3 [bdz]: \"Who descended from heaven\" (Or i yernits ijer). Barekendan of the Fast of Vardavar.\nSunday. Tone 3 [bdz]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The period of non-fasting is three weeks. See up to the Barekendan of the Assumption of the Mother of God in the First Volume; only look up the Sunday Fathers (Harts) here.\nSunday. Tone 2 [aki]. Second [Sunday]. Father (Harts) Tone 4 [bki]: \"Who of the heavenly hosts\" (Or yerknayin zinvorutyants). Hambartsi [Hymn of Ascent] Tone 2 [aki]: \"You were sent\" (Araketsar).\n\nAugust\n\nSunday. Tone 1 [adz]. Third [Sunday]. Father (Harts) Tone 7 [gdz]: \"We glorify\" (Paravoremp).\nSunday. Tone 8 [dki]. Fourth [Sunday]. Father (Harts) Tone 6 [gki]: \"Ineffable\" (Anchareli). Barekendan of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God.\nMonday. Tone 1 [adz]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Father (Harts) Tone 3 [bdz]: \"Blessed are you, Lord God of our fathers.\"\nSunday. Tone 7 [gdz]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The period of non-fasting is three weeks. See according to the order in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nSeptember\n\nSunday. Tone 4 [bki]. Fourth [Sunday]. Feast of the Nativity of the Holy Mother of God from Anna.\nBarekendan of the Holy Cross.\nMonday. Tone 7 [gdz]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Father (Harts) Tone 4 [bki]: \"The captive youths\" (Mankunkn geryalk).\nSunday. Tone 4 [bki]. Exaltation of the Cross [Khachverats]. See in the First Volume up to the tenth Sunday, keeping the order of this place.\nSunday. Tone 2 [aki]. Second [Sunday]. Hambartsi [Hymn of Ascent] Tone 2 [aki]: \"Risen\" (Harutsyal). Barekendan of the Cross of Varag.\nMonday. Tone 3 [bdz]. Fast of Mamas, etc. Father (Harts) Tone 8 [dki]: \"To you, O God\" (Ar kez astuadz).\nWednesday. Tone 7 [gdz]. Fast. Father (Harts) Tone 7 [gdz]: \"Glorified is your name\" (Paravoryal e anun ko).\nSunday. Tone 1 [adz]. Third [Sunday]. Feast of the Holy Cross of Varag. The period of non-fasting is seven weeks.\n\nOctober\n\nSunday. Tone 8 [dki]. Fourth [Sunday]. Hambartsi [Hymn of Ascent] Tone 8 [dki]: \"The hosts of angels\" (Hreshtakatsn dask).",
